A||N||6||Vlad||Gas leak||||3||
Z||000000||Vlad||09-21-2000||04:38 PM||||Hello<P>I guess I found the reason for my bad mileage. I was getting about 15 mpg. I've checked almost everything and replaced all suspicious parts, but nothing helped.<BR>So what I found was a leak in one of the fuel lines. The exact place of leak is under the plenum where the line is attached to that thing with a Shredder(sp?) valve on it.<BR>It seems to be leaking from the nut that holds the line. <BR>When the engine is not running, the place of leak is clean and dry. No smell. However, once the motor is on, the nut holding the line in becomes wet. You even can see the big drip staying on it. <BR>Since it's wet all the time engine is running, I assume that gas is constantly leaking when under pressure (45 psi...??).<BR>It seems to be a good explanation for  bad gas mileage, does it?<BR>Now... How do I fix it?<P>The metal line itself is short and, in case I find another one, can be easily replaced. I think I even don't have to take plenum off. Are those lines available in parts stores?<BR>But if the problem is a tread in that thing with valve, then how can I replace it? Can it be separated from the fuel rail which holds injectors?<P>Anyway... Any input appreciated.<P>Vlad<BR> <P><BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Vlad||09-21-2000||10:17 PM||||Anything.......??<P>I really need an advise weather I should do it myself or take to somebody else...<P>||||reg||9
Z||000002||StuGood||09-22-2000||12:16 AM||||Obviously, the bigger concern is danger of fire, not just fuel economy.  I wouldn't delay fixing this problem if I were you!  You don't want to damage yourself, plus we wouldn't want give our Fieros the reputation of being little plastic firetraps, now would we?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <P>Personally, I would probably want to take the upper plenum off to service the fuel block.  Those threads in the fuel rail are aluminum, and they could crossthread/ strip pretty easily if you try to remove/replace the bolt without giving yourself adequate room.<P>Depressurize system by pulling fuel pump fuse, and crank engine until it won't restart. Wrap a rag around the area of the "shredder" (actually, Schraeder) valve, and press the valve stem unitl any fuel all runs out.  Don't squirt yourself in the eye!<P>Now you can remove the screw holding the  <BR>fuel block to the fuel rail.  Underneath you should find a seal.  My guess (hope?)is that this seal is the source of the leak - replace it with a new one.<P>Next check the fittings where they screw into the fuel block.  <P>If it turns out to be the actual fuel line leaking (as you suspected), you would want to replace it.  Hopefully GM can provide you with a new one.     <BR>  <P> ||||reg||4
Z||000003||Vlad||09-22-2000||01:05 AM||||Wow.....<P>Thank you very much.<BR>I'm going to fix it tomorrow.<P>The bottom line is that the fuel block (that thing with a Schraeder valve on it) can be taken off the fuel rail by unscrewing only one screw. It means that in worst case the only two things I will have to replace are the fuel block and the fuel line.<P>I will try to check the fuel line fitting first because the wet area is above fuel block seal. That's why I suspect fitting, but not a seal.<P>Thanks again<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||09-22-2000||01:05 PM||||Looks like two or three screws, not one, FWIW. And they are Torx head screws.<P>My mistake...  look at: <A HREF="http://www.fbody.com/members/redredconv/Mvc-024s.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fbody.com/members/redredconv/Mvc-024s.jpg</A> <P>Should be fairly easy, still.<BR>Good luck   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !<p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-22-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000005||Vlad||09-22-2000||11:10 PM||||So I did it.<P>I didn't take the plenum off.However, to gain access to the back fuel line I disconnected the front fuel line and removed one bolt that was sitting between lines. <BR>After that, the job was quite easy.<P>My problem was a bad O-ring seal. Changing it solved the leak.||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||09-23-2000||02:33 PM||||I'm glad, Vlad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> !||||reg||14
